{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"7efae8e621f91ef499558db6132688fc08528588b6936618a04c88bb022c83b2","packTokens":1228,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":206,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":485,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":431,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads).\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write its sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How many demo requests and what status/area coverage should SeedData.Run provide, given the product document specifies exactly eight but the implementation request asks for only a few contract-example rows?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Seed a few believable rows from the contract examples, without requiring eight rows or specified status and area counts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen if SeedData.Run is invoked more than once while demo seeding is enabled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not insert duplicate demo rows on repeated runs.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"For create-request validation, should the API implement only the validation and error details defined by the locked OpenAPI contract, or also enforce the product document’s explicit field limits and messages wherever they differ or are absent from the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use only the validation and errors defined by the locked OpenAPI contract.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"If PostgreSQL is unreachable, should the application fail during startup, or start successfully and fail only when an operation needs the database?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup when PostgreSQL cannot be reached; do not fall back to another store.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the existing GET / health endpoint remain alongside the four contract operations, or should it be removed so the API exposes only the operations in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the existing GET / health endpoint in addition to the four contract operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement the Maintenance Requests API so listing requests supports descending createdAt order, status filtering, contract-compliant errors, and the specified server-error response.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Implement request creation with trimmed title and description, system-assigned positive IDs, UTC timestamps, Open status, optional omitted blank descriptions, and the specified validation and failure responses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Implement retrieval of a request by ID with the specified success, not-found, and failure responses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Implement status updates allowing only Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open, with the specified validation, not-found, conflict, and failure responses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Persist requests in PostgreSQL using the configured App connection string so they remain available after a restart, and fail startup if PostgreSQL cannot be reached.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Implement an idempotent demo seeder that adds at least one row for each of the three selected contract examples, using generated positive IDs and UTC timestamps, and invoke it at startup if and only if Seed:Demo is true.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Keep the GET / health response as HTTP 200 with body \\\"API is up\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Do not provide maintenance-request screens or pages in the API repository; the screen-flow end-to-end test belongs in the separate web-app repository.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}